# Little Browser: tab groups among the pinned tabs (docs/ux.md §6.1). Chromium can't group pinned
# tabs, so chromium/lb keeps pinned groups itself, over Chromium's pinned tabs
# (lb/browser/ui/tabs/pinned_group_tracker.h). This hooks them in:
# - the vertical strip's pinned container lays out each group's header row, indents its tabs,
#   hides a collapsed group's tabs and draws its colour line (lb::PinnedGroupLayout), and tells it
#   where a dragged tab is drawn and where its place is, which decide the pinned group it is in;
# - a tab in a collapsed pinned group counts as collapsed (TabStripModel::IsTabCollapsed), as for
#   Ctrl+Tab;
# - a pinned group tab's group is saved as tab extra data, also when Chromium rebuilds its session
#   file and in tab restore's record of a closed tab or window, and a restored tab gets it back;
# - the tab menu's Add to New Group and Tab > Group Tab make a pinned group of pinned tabs (Group
#   Tab also takes them out again), and a today group's menu has Pin Group;
# - today groups dragged by their header over the pinned area show a line where they would be
#   pinned (lb::OnTabGroupDragged), and dropped above the middle of "+ New Tab" they become pinned
#   groups there, with any other dragged tabs (lb::OnTabGroupDropped); a cancelled drag gives its
#   tabs back their pinned groups (lb::OnTabDragEnded).
